TAB@Customer Service Demo

A Hebrew, right-to-left web demo of a customer-service representative screen in the TAB@Work product family. It uses a sample Nespresso support call to show how on-screen context and guidance could help a representative handle a machine issue and pass an escalating conversation to a shift manager.

## What the demo shows

- A representative view with a waiting-call queue, customer card, machine troubleshooting information, suggested wording, and escalation cues.
- A shift-manager view with the escalation context, recent transcript, and controls that illustrate joining the call, guiding the representative, and marking follow-up.
- A screen layout the representative can rearrange during the demo.

These are illustrated workflows in a demo, not a live customer-service system or a claim of production integrations.

## Run locally

Open `index.html` in a browser, or serve the repository root with any static file server. The repository contains prebuilt JavaScript and CSS under `assets/`; there is no package install or build step for these files.

## Deployment

The static site is hosted on Vercel: https://tab-call-service.vercel.app/

